metag: find the FDEs of shared libraries through dl_iterate_phdr

The Meta Linux target uses its own metag/t-linux instead of config/t-linux
and so never set LIB2ADDEH: libgcc was built with unwind-dw2-fde.c, which
only knows frames registered with __register_frame_info.  crtbegin.o does
that for the executable, but a library linked without it -- the C library
-- never registers its .eh_frame, so the unwinder found no FDE in it even
with PT_GNU_EH_FRAME present.  Unwinding into libc stopped there: a thread
cancelled in read() never got back to its cleanup handlers.

Take unwind-dw2-fde-glibc.c, as config/t-linux does.

--- a/gcc/config/metag/t-linux
+++ b/gcc/config/metag/t-linux
@@ -44,3 +44,10 @@
 # Don't make libgcc1-test since it will fail because it tries to link with liblow.a which doesn't exist for linux toolchain!
 LIBGCC1_TEST =
 
+
+# Find the FDEs of shared libraries through PT_GNU_EH_FRAME and
+# dl_iterate_phdr, as config/t-linux does: a library linked without crtbegin,
+# such as the C library, never registers its frames.
+LIB2ADDEH = $(srcdir)/unwind-dw2.c $(srcdir)/unwind-dw2-fde-glibc.c \
+  $(srcdir)/unwind-sjlj.c $(srcdir)/gthr-gnat.c $(srcdir)/unwind-c.c
+LIB2ADDEHDEP = unwind.inc unwind-dw2-fde.h unwind-dw2-fde.c
